  "thumbnailAlt": "Order Form form beside a photo of man packing blue coffee mugs for delivery in a bright, artistic workspace",
  "content": {
    "intro": "An order form is a form that collects a customer's contact details, the products and quantities they want, and how and when they want them delivered so a seller can fulfill the order correctly. This template works for small sellers without a web store: share one link, and every order arrives with the item list, delivery choice and notes in one place.",
    "audience": "Home bakers, caterers, craft and gift sellers, farm shops, print shops, school and club merchandise sellers, and wholesalers taking repeat orders.",
    "useCases": [
      "Pre-orders for holiday cakes, meal boxes or farm produce",
      "Team or club merchandise orders with sizes per item",
      "Wholesale reorders from regular trade customers",
      "Orders taken through Instagram or WhatsApp links instead of DMs"
    ],
    "tips": [
      "Put prices in the product option labels so customers see them while they order.",
      "Set a response limit or a closing time in Form Settings to stop orders when stock or your order window runs out.",
      "Use a PDF template to turn each order into a printable packing slip or order confirmation."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What should an order form include?",
        "answer": "The customer's name, email and phone; each product with quantity and size or variant; delivery or pickup; the delivery address; the date they need it; how they plan to pay; and a notes box for special requests. This template includes all of them."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can customers order several products in one form?",
        "answer": "Yes. This template has numbered product lines with their own quantity and variant fields, and you can add more lines in the builder. Conditional logic can hide extra lines until the customer needs them."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does this form take card details?",
        "answer": "No. It records the order and the customer's preferred way to pay. You then send an invoice or a pay link from the tool you already use, or collect on pickup."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I stop orders after a cutoff date?",
        "answer": "Set a close time in Form Settings. After that time the form shows a closed message, so late orders do not arrive after your production deadline."
      }
    ]
  },
